WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.957
The database contains a few small source areas.

00:00:02.957 --> 00:00:06.527
Patient and admission tables support healthcare-style views.

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:11.207
Employee, department, and sales-order tables support a performance interface.

00:00:11.207 --> 00:00:15.482
Customer transactions support recent-activity and retention examples.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:22.597
Reusable objects are placed in an analytics schema so the source tables and analytical interfaces are clearly

00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:28.382
separated. Connect this idea to a data platform materializing expensive summaries for faster consumption.

00:00:28.382 --> 00:00:33.537
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.537 --> 00:00:40.447
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:40.447 --> 00:00:44.252
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:49.520
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
